{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_payment_flow_payment_flow", "label": "Payment flow (O1-O8, P1-P12)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Supersedes the payment sequence in architecture.md \u00a74.1. No pre-established payer-payee link is required: B2B reality is paying an invoice from a supplier you have never paid, and forcing a two-sided link first is a chicken-and-egg problem for no gain, because the identity binding rather than the relationship defeats a tampered address."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_address_untrusted_routing", "label": "The address is untrusted routing; the identity is the verification", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The sender pastes an address off an invoice \u2014 exactly where hijacking lives \u2014 and states who they intend to pay, so a tampered address is caught by being bound to a different DigiLocker subject."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_consent_gates_verification", "label": "Consent gates verification, and verification gates money", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nothing is verified until the receiver agrees to be verified, and no money moves until verification passes \u2014 verifying after settlement is detect-and-refund, which banks already do. Consent is also the primary throttle, because each probe costs the victim's active acceptance."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_onboarding_sequence", "label": "Onboarding O1-O8", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "O2, O4 and O7 prove who, key possession, and personhood/continuity respectively; none substitutes for another."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_digest_matching", "label": "Digest matching in the enclave (D62)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "There is no crypto in the CRE enclave \u2014 node:crypto is banned by the SDK's restricted-modules list and no crypto.subtle global exists \u2014 so 'encrypt at rest, decrypt inside the enclave' has no primitive. Comparing HMAC digests as opaque bytes sidesteps it and the pepper never leaves the server. The cost is the near-miss band: exact-after-normalisation is stricter and defeats lookalike payees, but a reviewer can no longer tell a typo from a different company; a mismatch costs a retry, never money. One reason code for any identity mismatch, because per-field errors would give a prober a second bit."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_evaluatematch", "label": "evaluateMatch() shared match rule", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Shared by the fallback, the TEE handler and the DON handler precisely so they cannot drift \u2014 if the fallback kept fuzzy scoring while CRE compared digests, the shared contract suite would stop proving anything about the CRE path."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_sender_world_id_gate", "label": "P2 sender World ID check, every payment", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Signal = paymentId and the proof must match the sender's enrolment nullifier, so a live continuous human is provably the one raising this specific payment; enforced in the service, since request-consent refuses without it (D64)."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_payee_consent", "label": "P3/P4 payee notification and EIP-712 consent", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DENY terminates with no match run and no funds moved; ACCEPT is signed by the CONFIRMED wallet with amount, token and invoiceRef inside the signed payload. runDecision refuses without an ACCEPTED consent, enforced in the service rather than by convention (D63), and the consent route is deliberately unauthenticated because the signature is the authorisation."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_payee_challenge_triggers", "label": "P5 payee challenge triggers (risk-based)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Detects a stolen key: a thief can sign the consent and claim the funds but cannot produce the nullifier. Enrolment at O7 is what matters \u2014 it makes the challenge available the moment something looks wrong."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_cre_confidential_workflow", "label": "P6 CRE confidential workflow (TEE digest comparison)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The enclave compares opaque digests so no plaintext identity ever enters it; NO_MATCH blocks and alerts the payee that someone claimed them and was wrong, which makes probing visible instead of silent."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_decision_engine", "label": "P7 decision engine gates", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sanctions, duplicate invoice, wallet CONFIRMED, tier ceiling, freshness (DigiLocker TTL, credential expiry, 90-day selfie window) and on-chain KYC granted."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_htlc_lock", "label": "P9-P11 HTLC lock / claim / refund", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The lock is the first movement of money and the preimage reveal IS the acknowledgment, so settlement and acknowledgment are atomic; no claim before the timelock refunds and opens an exception."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_one_bit_leak", "label": "Known residual: the one-bit leak", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Irreducible for any check that decides whether to pay; throttled rather than eliminated because every probe needs the target to actively accept a payment request and generates a mismatch alert, so twenty probes is twenty prompts to one person who then blocks the sender."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_invoice_fraud_defence", "label": "Why invoice fraud fails", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The sender can be fully tricked into pasting the attacker's address and still not lose the money, because the claimed PAN mismatches the address's KYC'd identity. To receive at all the attacker must complete DigiLocker KYC, so invoice fraud stops being free and anonymous and starts costing a real, traceable, prosecutable identity revocable across every buyer at once \u2014 structural, not a tunable policy. Escrow-as-deterrent and punitive deductions were deliberately rejected."}, {"id": "docs_payment_flow_assurance_boundaries", "label": "Assurance boundaries \u2014 do not overclaim", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Selfie Check is medium assurance and proves the same human as enrolled, never which human; EIP-712 proves key possession, not personhood; DigiLocker proves legal identity, only as fresh as its TTL."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_payment_flow_payment_flow", "target": "docs_payment_flow_address_untrusted_routing", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_payment_flow_payment_flow", "target": "docs_payment_flow_consent_gates_verification", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_payment_flow_payment_flow", "target": "docs_payment_flow_onboarding_sequence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_payment_flow_onboarding_sequence", "target": "docs_architecture_identity_binding", "relation": "references", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_payment_flow_onboarding_sequence", "target": "docs_architecture_digilockerprovider", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_payment_flow_digest_matching", "target": "docs_payment_flow_evaluatematch", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/payment-flow.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_payment_flow_evaluatematch", "target": "docs_architecture_vendormatcher", "relation": "impleme